.0; 138 edges retired, 77 new edges), and turnover rises from a ~0.25 baseline to 1.0 only in a narrow band around 77986 before relaxing, indicating a short transition rather than gradual drift. Volume, per-node degree uniformity, and the mirrored switch in the old-partner set rule out sparsity, single-node bursts, and hub popularity as explanations.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 32404, "total_output_tokens": 2859, "total_tokens": 35263, "total_latency_ms": 50791, "llm_calls": 5, "schema_repairs": 0, "tool_protocol_errors": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}